NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "Mixin::Linewise - write your linewise code for handles; this does the rest"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "version 0.111"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "It's boring to deal with opening files for IO, converting strings to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "handle-like objects, and all that.  With L<Mixin::Linewise::Readers> and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "L<Mixin::Linewise::Writers>, you can just write a method to handle handles, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "methods for handling strings and filenames are added for you."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "=head1 PERL VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "This module should work on any version of perl still receiving updates from"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "the Perl 5 Porters.  This means it should work on any version of perl released"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "in the last two to three years.  (That is, if the most recently released"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "version is v5.40, then this module should work on both v5.40 and v5.38.)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "Although it may work on older versions of perl, no guarantee is made that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "minimum required version will not be increased.  The version may be increased"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 "for any reason, and there is no promise that patches will be accepted to lower"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "the minimum required perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
